From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: aw88395: allow a speaker id strap

The Lenovo TB375FC has speakers from two suppliers with their own tuning
files. A GPIO strap tells them apart, read by all four amplifiers.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/sound/awinic,aw88395.yaml      | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/awinic,aw88395.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/awinic,aw88395.yaml
index b9abb10..8729868 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/awinic,aw88395.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/awinic,aw88395.yaml
@@ -36,8 +36,16 @@ properties:
   dvdd-supply: true
 
   firmware-name:
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 2
+    description:
+      Name of the *_acf.bin file used for amplifier initialization. With
+      awinic,speaker-id-gpios, the name that the GPIO's value selects.
+
+  awinic,speaker-id-gpios:
     maxItems: 1
-    description: Name of the *_acf.bin file used for amplifier initialization
+    description:
+      A strap that tells which speakers the board has, shared by its amplifiers.
 
   awinic,audio-channel:
     description:
